From 54426cf1e7459b0d1e9b6b62e6ddac36eab417ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:52:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0315 -- composite world cache, stage 3b
 (tile-aligned key)

Stage 3b: consult a key so an unchanged frame skips the composite entirely
and goes straight to the read-out blit. This is where the saving arrives;
3a was pure cost by construction.

The key is TILE-ALIGNED, which is the specific fix for patch 0097. 0097
keyed on pixel scroll and therefore missed on every single pixel of camera
motion; its break-even was a 0.92 hit rate it never approached. Keying on
the tile-aligned origin means a hit survives 15 of every 16 pixels of camera
travel, because the sub-tile remainder is applied at read-out rather than
baked into the composite. Break-even here is 0.33.

Gated separately from the 3a hint so ONE binary carries all three arms:
neither hint = uncached baseline, WORLD_CACHE=1 = 3a unconditional
composite, WORLD_CACHE=1 + WORLD_CACHE_KEY=1 = 3b keyed. Three arms on one
reel makes attribution a within-binary comparison instead of a cross-binary
one, which this campaign has repeatedly found unreliable.

Key fields and why each is present: curmap (different content, reloads
tilesets), tile-aligned mapx/mapy, tile_mutation, window surface pointer
(re-fetch invalidates the blit target), and screen dimensions. Animated
tiles (TA_CURRENT) and destroyables (0x43) are excluded from the composite
and render live, so animation must not and does not invalidate. The backdrop
is not cached under variant B, so no backdrop or parallax phase belongs
here.

FIXES A LATENT STALE-TILE BUG. Patch 0097 bumped g_tile_mutation_counter in
map_ChangeTileWithSmoke ONLY. TSC <CMP and the Hell stage write map.tiles
directly and never bumped it -- harmless while 0097's cache was default-OFF
and never hit, a stale-tile defect the moment a cache can actually hit.
Patch 0144 had already identified TSC <CMP as the second mutation site for
the mds_clear LUT without connecting it to the tilemap counter. All three
sites now route through map_note_tile_mutation(), which bumps the counter
and drops the validity flag.

Counters are real. The plan's sec. 1.1 found tm_route_cache was a literal
carrying only killswitch state, which misled every reader of the Round N
logs. A hit rate that cannot be read from the log is not a measurement, so
the per-100-frame line reports hits, composites, declines and hit_pct_x10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
